        "language": "c",
        "author": "IARPA STONESOUP Test and Evaluation team",
        "description": "This test case takes a filename. It determines the size of the file, and attempts to check whether the size of the file is smaller than 128 characters. The arithmetic used in the if-check may cause an integer underflow, which will result in the if-check succeeding when it should fail. If the if-check succeeds after an integer underflow, a large amount of data is copied into a small (128-character) buffer on the stack. This will overwrite memory on the stack, resulting in segmentation fault upon return from the function.\nMetadata\n - Base program: PostgreSQL\n - Source Taint: SOCKET\n - Data Type: SIMPLE\n - Data Flow: ADDRESS_AS_LINEAR_EXPRESSION\n - Control Flow: INTERPROCEDURAL_50",
        "state": "bad",
        "application": "cpe:2.3:a:postgresql:postgresql:9.2.4:*:*:*:*:*:*:*",
        "dependencies": [
